Will,

I personally mind if we give individual people write access to the sources if
they appear to have serious interest to work, creating spinoffs is not really
going to help I guess.

On the other hand some sort of proof of knowledge/quality and also some
indication that not everything is being messed up without some prior
consultation and agreement would be kind of helpful. Now all that might be
difficult to ensure with a person that isn't really known in the scene so to
speak.

On the other hand why not give it a try and see how this works out. Or we wait
a little and just freeze l3doc in the svn and you two work a little longside
and if you get the impression that this works out we open up the svn for him.

Up to you I would say, I would support either way

frank
